1
00:00:10,630 --> 00:00:14,480
As you know, your stepbrother Nick is
actually coming back from college soon.

2
00:00:14,481 --> 00:00:16,640
Oh my gosh, it's been so long.

3
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:18,000
It's been like two years.

4
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:20,280
It's been too long.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,480
I haven't had a chance to go visit him.

6
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:23,880
He hasn't had time to come down.

7
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:26,400
So he's finally coming back in a few days.

8
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,960
I'm so excited.

9
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:34,400
But this place is such a mess and I need your
help to help, you know, tidy it up a little bit.

10
00:00:34,401 --> 00:00:37,300
I want to make it nice and spick
and span for when he gets home.

11
00:00:37,690 --> 00:00:41,940
So I need your help sweeping,
dusting, we need to scrub the floors.

12
00:00:42,519 --> 00:00:46,600
And I was hoping if you wouldn't mind
helping me tidy up his room a little bit.

13
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:47,740
Yeah, yeah.

14
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,076
I think you can help me with that.

15
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:50,740
Yeah, and mop and everything.

16
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:51,900
Yeah.

17
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:53,520
Anything for little Nicky.

18
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:54,960
Of course, of course.

19
00:00:54,980 --> 00:00:57,520
And I mean, I cannot wait for him to get
here.

20
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,060
I know, I'm so excited.

21
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:02,940
If you don't mind helping me tidy up his room,
I'll go get started on the kitchen stuff, okay?

22
00:01:02,941 --> 00:01:04,060
Yeah, definitely.

23
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:05,459
Thank you so much, sweetie.

24
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,600
Of course.

25
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:42,340
Gotta have the place spick and span for
Nicky.

26
00:02:13,864 --> 00:02:14,640
Surprise!

27
00:02:14,641 --> 00:02:14,740
Oh my gosh.

28
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:15,900
Oh my gosh.

29
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:17,460
Is that my stepson?

30
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:18,420
It's me.

31
00:02:18,660 --> 00:02:18,980
I'm home.

32
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:19,700
Oh my gosh.

33
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,100
It is.

34
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,640
Welcome home.

35
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:24,320
Thank you.

36
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:25,460
It's so good to be home.

37
00:02:25,660 --> 00:02:26,660
You're here so early.

38
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,720
Well, I mean, I got all the courses done.

39
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,896
Got the exams out of the way.

40
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,720
No reason to stick around.

41
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:31,860
So here I am.

42
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:32,160
Aw.

43
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,300
You're such a good boy.

44
00:02:33,301 --> 00:02:34,440
I'm so proud of you.

45
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:35,900
Aw.

46
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:38,940
I mean, it's really good to be back.

47
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,540
Well, we weren't expecting you for two
more days.

48
00:02:41,541 --> 00:02:43,760
We were just doing some spring cleaning
for you.

49
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:44,500
Oh, really?

50
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:44,900
Oh.

51
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:45,980
Yeah.

52
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:47,290
Should I go back?

53
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:48,670
Oh, no.

54
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,300
Not at all.

55
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,480
I'm cleaning your room for you right now.

56
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:52,060
Oh, really?

57
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,240
Oh, thank you.

58
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:53,580
Yeah.

59
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:55,320
Oh, you both are so amazing.

60
00:02:55,640 --> 00:02:55,720
Yeah.

61
00:02:55,721 --> 00:02:56,860
I really appreciate it.

62
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:57,260
Thank you.

63
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:01,260
So, I'll just go and like kick back for a
bit.

64
00:03:01,810 --> 00:03:02,810
While we finish up.

65
00:03:03,060 --> 00:03:03,640
Is that all right?

66
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:04,700
That sounds perfect.

67
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:07,500
That was a long trip, so... No, no worries.

68
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,600
Go relax.

69
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,360
Shit.

70
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,340
Well, just go get settled in, honey.

71
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:37,160
We're going to be cleaning up for you,
okay?

72
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:37,680
All right.

73
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,760
Thanks, Mom.

74
00:03:40,234 --> 00:03:41,234
Hey, Mom.

75
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,100
We're going to have some stuff on the
machine.

76
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,600
Okay.

77
00:03:45,364 --> 00:03:49,500
Do you want me to toss you any of my
laundry out of the bag or just leave it for now?

78
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:50,340
Oh, no, man.

79
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,440
Don't let the finger.

80
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:53,040
Okay.

81
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,320
Thanks.

82
00:03:57,644 --> 00:03:59,040
So, how was your flight, hon?

83
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:00,840
It wasn't that bad.

84
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,800
It took a lot, but you know, it is what it
is.

85
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:04,640
Yeah.

86
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:05,380
Yep.

87
00:04:05,381 --> 00:04:06,580
Was there any crying babies?

88
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:07,260
I hate that.

89
00:04:07,261 --> 00:04:08,020
No.

90
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:11,660
There was a crying old
woman, which was kind of weird.

91
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:13,660
She was very noisy.

92
00:04:14,204 --> 00:04:15,204
Oh, jeez.

93
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,000
I hate those.

94
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:18,180
Did you get to have any
snacks or anything like that?

95
00:04:18,725 --> 00:04:19,725
They had pretzels.

96
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:20,300
They were all right.

97
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:21,420
They were unsalted.

98
00:04:22,455 --> 00:04:23,855
Well, that doesn't sound very good.

99
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:25,240
We'll have to get you some dinner.

100
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:25,920
Oh, yeah.

101
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,120
What are you making?

102
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:27,520
Hmm.

103
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,040
Lasagna, spaghetti?

104
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:29,660
What would you prefer?

105
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:30,520
Oh, lasagna sounds good.

106
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,300
Oh, good.

107
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:31,680
Perfect.

108
00:04:31,681 --> 00:04:32,681
Yeah, let's do that.

109
00:04:33,540 --> 00:04:34,540
Green cheese?

110
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:35,640
Of course.

111
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:36,740
Yes.

112
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,980
You know, I really missed you,
Mom.

113
00:04:39,860 --> 00:04:40,080
Yeah.

114
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:41,500
It's really good to see you.

115
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:42,580
It's been too long.

116
00:04:42,705 --> 00:04:44,200
Aw, it's good to see you too, right?

117
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:46,320
Mm-hmm.

118
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,380
You've always been a great student,
though.

119
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,220
I try.

120
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,560
No problem.

121
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,260
Well, you know, education's important.

122
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:55,100
Mm, that it is.

123
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,620
Almost as important as family.

124
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,480
That's the most important.

125
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,120
Hm.

126
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,080
And your friends, how's Sam doing?

127
00:05:13,695 --> 00:05:14,800
Sam's doing great.

128
00:05:15,020 --> 00:05:18,140
He got a scholarship at that
other IVB college over in Georgia.

129
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:19,220
Oh, wow.

130
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:20,440
Yeah, I know.

131
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,760
Good for him, right?

132
00:05:21,761 --> 00:05:22,761
Good for him.

133
00:05:22,975 --> 00:05:24,215
I'm sure his parents are proud.

134
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,760
Yeah, they are.

135
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:27,130
They got him a new car.

136
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:28,340
Oh, wow.

137
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:29,600
Not just any new car.

138
00:05:30,355 --> 00:05:33,420
That sports car he was going on and
on about the other time he was over.

139
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:34,340
Oh, my God.

140
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,020
Well, you know, he deserves it.

141
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,300
He does.

142
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,420
He works so hard on his grades.

143
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,640
Mm, yeah.

144
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,600
But, like, what has been going on here?

145
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:49,220
Like, Fiona's been busy or what?

146
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:50,380
Uh, you know what?

147
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:52,120
She's been deep in her studies.

148
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:53,540
Really?

149
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,180
She was never really that much of a
studier.

150
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,360
That's good to hear.

151
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,180
Well, I think she's taking
after-taking a cue from you.

152
00:06:00,620 --> 00:06:01,620
Ha.

153
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,840
Well, I'm glad to be a positive influence.

154
00:06:08,965 --> 00:06:10,805
I think she just wants to get out of the
house.

155
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:12,360
Trying to escape.

156
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:24,161
Truth be told, I wouldn't mind another- another
kid that's just as well behaved as you are.

157
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,240
Oh, Mom.

158
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:26,400
Mm-hmm.

159
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:30,470
No, I mean, I try.

160
00:06:30,970 --> 00:06:31,370
Mm-hmm.

161
00:06:31,765 --> 00:06:33,750
If you do good things, good things come to
you.

162
00:06:34,070 --> 00:06:35,070
Mm.

163
00:06:35,485 --> 00:06:36,830
That's very true, son.

164
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,160
Mm-hmm.

165
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:47,530
So, how long have you been
working on that project for?

166
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:50,900
Um, you know, it's gonna be about two
months now.

167
00:06:51,415 --> 00:06:53,040
Oh, wow, now you're finishing it up.

168
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:53,600
Yes.

169
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:54,920
Must be a big project.

170
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,900
I am so excited to be done with it.

171
00:06:57,260 --> 00:06:57,340
Hmm.

172
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,260
That's cool.

173
00:06:58,539 --> 00:07:00,160
These clients are driving me insane.

174
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:01,480
So, what do you think?

175
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:03,196
You're gonna have some more free time
after that?

176
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:03,840
Oh, definitely.

177
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:04,500
Hopefully.

178
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:05,840
That's cool.

179
00:07:06,850 --> 00:07:07,970
I'm gonna get this calendar.

180
00:07:08,055 --> 00:07:09,920
I'm gonna get this calendar.

181
00:07:10,810 --> 00:07:11,810
You dare to dream.

182
00:07:14,450 --> 00:07:16,000
And yeah, living the dream.

183
00:07:23,485 --> 00:07:25,210
Well, it's definitely nice to be back
home.

184
00:07:25,310 --> 00:07:27,330
And be even nicer to have more time with
you.

185
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:28,690
Mm-hmm.

186
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,710
Well, let's plan on that this time.

187
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,250
Yeah, let's definitely plan on it.

188
00:07:33,251 --> 00:07:34,251
Okay.

189
00:07:39,295 --> 00:07:40,455
So, what about Fiona, though?

190
00:07:40,905 --> 00:07:42,720
She been, like, dating or anything?

191
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:44,300
Have any boys around?

192
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,400
One guy, one week.

193
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:48,120
And another girl, another week.

194
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,500
I mean, I just... Jesus.

195
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:50,620
I can't keep up.

196
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:51,710
She gets around.

197
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:52,240
I know.

198
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:53,780
Well, you know your sister.

199
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:55,280
I don't blame her.

200
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:56,390
Quite the party animal.

201
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:57,600
I blame them, I guess.

202
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,020
Mm-hmm.

203
00:07:59,930 --> 00:08:04,560
Well, maybe we'll... Maybe I'll get
to meet the next one she brings, huh?

204
00:08:04,561 --> 00:08:05,000
Yeah.

205
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,180
Maybe.

206
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:07,320
Just give it a day.

207
00:08:08,085 --> 00:08:09,085
Give it a day?

208
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:11,936
Don't tell me she gets around that one.

209
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:13,580
Oh, well... I know your sister.

210
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,840
She likes to party, but she's a good girl.

211
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:18,220
Well, you did say she's
working on her studies more.

212
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:18,700
Yeah.

213
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:19,580
So, that's good.

214
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,000
She seems a lot more focused.

215
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:22,380
Well, that's important.

216
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,960
It's good to be goal-oriented.

217
00:08:25,849 --> 00:08:28,000
So, what are her plans, though,
for college?

218
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:30,321
Is she trying to... What's she trying to do?

219
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:34,539
Um, you know, I think she said
something about being a doctor.

220
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:34,840
A doctor?

221
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:35,679
A doctor?

222
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,299
A vet?

223
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:37,559
Yeah.

224
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:58,750
Ugh.

225
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,660
I'm so glad you're home.

226
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:04,140
I'm too.

227
00:09:04,180 --> 00:09:05,700
I've been gone for way too long.

228
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:06,120
Yeah.

229
00:09:06,121 --> 00:09:06,160
I've been down for a while.

230
00:09:06,161 --> 00:09:07,161
Yeah.

231
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:09,030
Ooh.

232
00:09:16,509 --> 00:09:17,870
I need this for Christmas.

233
00:09:36,089 --> 00:09:37,089
Hey Fiona?

234
00:09:38,219 --> 00:09:39,560
How's that laundry coming?

235
00:09:41,490 --> 00:09:42,720
Oh, what's going on?

236
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,020
I'm just gonna show up, phone a few
things.

237
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:47,780
I see Nick's really back.

238
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I am.

239
00:09:50,999 --> 00:09:53,280
Hey mom, I'm going to do my stepbrother's
sheets.

240
00:09:58,620 --> 00:09:58,980
Okay.

241
00:09:58,981 --> 00:10:01,580
Well, Ashley, do you want to
clean some of those dishes?

242
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:03,016
There's a few of them left in there.

243
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:03,120
Yeah.

244
00:10:03,121 --> 00:10:04,641
If you don't mind getting that for me.

245
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:05,800
Thank you, love.

246
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,660
It's so nice to have the whole family
home.

247
00:10:09,960 --> 00:10:10,500
I know.

248
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:10,940
I know.

249
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,460
All under one roof.

250
00:10:12,461 --> 00:10:13,461
Uh-huh.

251
00:10:23,189 --> 00:10:24,640
So how was college, man?

252
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:25,180
It was good.

253
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:27,940
I learned a lot of things, met a lot of
people.

254
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:31,280
Definitely, definitely experiences.

255
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:32,880
Yeah?

256
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:34,900
How's the party scene out there?

257
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:40,780
You know me, I've always had that kind of a book
warrant, so... I've had some crazy professors.

258
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:41,720
Did you?

259
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,280
Yeah.

260
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:47,800
Oh yeah, that's right.

261
00:10:47,870 --> 00:10:49,070
We're taking some AP classes.

262
00:10:49,071 --> 00:10:50,071
Yeah.

263
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,330
And how has this been going?

264
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,190
Pretty good.

265
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,770
A lot of years of school.

266
00:10:59,510 --> 00:11:00,510
Oh yeah.

267
00:11:01,190 --> 00:11:02,910
Gonna be there for a long time.

268
00:11:05,630 --> 00:11:08,050
But at least I have the party to keep me
going.

269
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:10,250
You're ridiculous.

270
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:12,070
I've missed you.

271
00:11:12,570 --> 00:11:14,330
I know, I really missed you.

272
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:17,930
It's great to have you back around the
house.

273
00:11:17,931 --> 00:11:19,270
It's really great to be back.

274
00:11:20,830 --> 00:11:21,830
It's not too long.

275
00:11:22,070 --> 00:11:23,070
It's who he is.

276
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:25,470
Well, you know, I had to go back in a few
months.

277
00:11:25,765 --> 00:11:26,765
I'm not done yet.

278
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,390
That's unfortunate.

279
00:11:28,510 --> 00:11:30,630
